    "result_text": "Tests are green. I agree with the finding and addressed it.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe review was correct: generic E.164 presentation logic and a calling-code registry are at the wrong altitude for a JPA entity. I extracted it:\n\n- **New `util/TelephoneFormatter.java`** \u2014 a final, non-instantiable helper holding the `KNOWN_CALLING_CODES` table and the `toDisplay(String)` method (longest-prefix country-code match + digit grouping). This sits alongside the existing `EntityUtils` in the util package, is independently testable, and is reusable by any holder of a telephone value.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 `getTelephoneDisplay()` is now a thin `@Transient` delegate: `return TelephoneFormatter.toDisplay(this.telephone);`. Removed the static list and the inline algorithm; added the import. The entity change is now a clean, additive getter.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 unchanged, as the finding noted it's fine as-is.\n\nBehaviour is identical (same algorithm, just relocated). Full `./mvnw -o test`: **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests green, including `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`).",
